  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The equation of the tangent to the curve $y=b e^{-x/a}$ at the point where it crosses the $y$ -axis is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "SwkRG",
      "text": "$\\frac{x}{a}-\\frac{y}{b}=1$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "0wAgK",
      "text": "$a x+b y=1$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "kjguC",
      "text": "$a x-b y=1$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "glVf5",
      "text": "$\\frac{x}{a}+\\frac{y}{b}=1$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "$y=b e^{-x / a}$ meets the $y$ -axis at $(0, b)$. Again,\r\n\r\n$\\frac{d y}{d x}=b e^{-x / a}\\left(-\\frac{1}{a}\\right)$\r\n\r\n$\\operatorname{At}(0, b), \\frac{d y}{d x}=b e^{0}\\left(-\\frac{1}{a}\\right)=-\\frac{b}{a}$\r\n\r\nTherefore, required tangent is\r\n\r\n$y-b=-\\frac{b}{a}(x-0) \\text { or } \\frac{x}{a}+\\frac{y}{b}=1$",
    "image": null
  },
